    <h1>Forest depth.<br>Slow crossings.</h1>
    <p class="hero-copy">Every study is a dense kelp forest with folded mid-rib blades, a drifting camera, and its own composition: clumped stands, open corridors, solid walls, or scattered islands. Some sit on jagged terrain, some on ground sloping up toward the surface, and some stay in open mid-water. Colors identify species—not scenes: blue-green ribbon kelp, jade fans, deep green feathers, and olive-gold bulb kelp mix through every forest.</p>
